1
00:02:09,189 --> 00:02:15,169
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:03:46,530 --> 00:03:47,960
Malhun.

3
00:03:50,835 --> 00:03:52,115
Come on.

4
00:04:46,903 --> 00:04:48,313
Come on Malhun!

5
00:05:41,077 --> 00:05:42,337
Where are you headed?

6
00:05:47,373 --> 00:05:50,533
Many will bleed today.

7
00:06:00,499 --> 00:06:02,779
A day ago.

8
00:06:05,363 --> 00:06:08,263
I will go to talk to
Manuel, the governor of Iznik, brother.

9
00:06:09,103 --> 00:06:12,893
I am going to use trading to vanish them,
just like the way they want to vanish us.

10
00:06:14,236 --> 00:06:17,626
I am going to offer him an opportunity
that none of the Lords would.

11
00:06:19,272 --> 00:06:21,582
He is going to take it if he is smart.

12
00:06:22,242 --> 00:06:25,502
He is going to face me if he is an idiot.

13
00:06:27,537 --> 00:06:30,277
A man rises with his respondent, my Bey.

14
00:06:31,064 --> 00:06:35,674
This agreement we are going to make with
the governor of Iznik will...

15
00:06:35,674 --> 00:06:37,384
...enhance the trust level of Kayi Tent.

16
00:06:38,654 --> 00:06:41,734
Osman Bey, all well and good but...

17
00:06:42,577 --> 00:06:44,717
This is going to drive Lords crazy, right?

18
00:06:45,059 --> 00:06:47,699
Lords are like rapid dogs, my Bala.

19
00:06:48,005 --> 00:06:52,305
A wolf becomes a wolf when one thousand
dogs bark at him.

20
00:06:54,603 --> 00:06:58,043
Infidels don't need reason to attack.

21
00:06:58,700 --> 00:07:01,420
Their hostility is eternal.

22
00:07:01,752 --> 00:07:06,342
They don't want us to settle down here,
to make this land our motherland.

23
00:07:08,744 --> 00:07:13,984
This is why my Osman is going to
ruin them inside.

24
00:07:14,571 --> 00:07:16,401
Evelallah (for sure).

25
00:07:17,442 --> 00:07:20,822
My Bey, I want to join you if you allow.

26
00:07:36,557 --> 00:07:38,337
Make preparations.

27
00:07:40,902 --> 00:07:45,032
My Bey, the road is dangerous.

28
00:07:45,714 --> 00:07:48,744
Lords must have heard you'll be on your
way to the governor.

29
00:07:51,537 --> 00:07:53,347
Also, Malhun Hatun is with you.

30
00:07:55,130 --> 00:07:57,550
I am worried that they may ambush you.

31
00:07:58,062 --> 00:08:02,602
Our swords are hammered by heat, covered
with the blood of infidels, Bala Hatun.

32
00:08:04,646 --> 00:08:07,336
We are going to overcome anything with
my Bey, Inshallah.

33
00:08:16,171 --> 00:08:19,311
My Bey, what about the relic?

34
00:08:21,922 --> 00:08:23,822
I am not taking it with me.

35
00:08:24,348 --> 00:08:28,038
I'll have a different path from
the regular Iznik path.

36
00:08:41,058 --> 00:08:42,259
Baykurt.

37
00:08:43,722 --> 00:08:46,542
Prepare the horseshoe.
It's Osman Bey's command.

38
00:08:50,234 --> 00:08:52,714
We are going to use Kızılhisar path
tomorrow.

39
00:08:52,714 --> 00:08:55,034
The path will be rocky.

40
00:08:55,075 --> 00:08:56,735
Eyvallah Head Alp.

41
00:08:58,549 --> 00:09:02,219
Baykurt, no one should hear this.

42
00:09:02,303 --> 00:09:03,863
Eyvallah (okay).

43
00:09:08,524 --> 00:09:11,934
Orhan is entrusted to me, Malhun Hatun.
Don't worry.

44
00:09:11,961 --> 00:09:14,101
May Allah bless you, Bala Hatun.

45
00:09:14,657 --> 00:09:17,847
Long live my Bala, long live.

46
00:09:18,541 --> 00:09:20,701
Can I come in my Bey?

47
00:09:21,075 --> 00:09:22,855
Come.

48
00:09:27,357 --> 00:09:29,787
I felt he wanted you, my Hatun.

49
00:09:32,915 --> 00:09:35,659
I am starting the preparations for tomorrow,
Osman Bey.

50
00:09:35,659 --> 00:09:37,819
I am going to set off.

51
00:09:38,813 --> 00:09:40,763
The relic will stay in the tent.

52
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:43,259
Listen to me carefully.

53
00:09:43,259 --> 00:09:48,519
It's your responsibility to protect
the tent, the relic, and my Orhan.

54
00:09:50,050 --> 00:09:52,030
As you command, Osman Bey.

55
00:10:07,601 --> 00:10:09,391
Tell me Gokce girl.

56
00:10:09,399 --> 00:10:12,309
I heard that the relic
is staying in the tent.

57
00:10:12,869 --> 00:10:14,709
Good job, Gokce.

58
00:10:23,404 --> 00:10:25,144
Keep your eyes open.

59
00:10:25,770 --> 00:10:29,620
Don't forget, they are going to be
punished for what they've done to you.

60
00:11:20,553 --> 00:11:22,843
Fly then.

61
00:11:23,156 --> 00:11:25,006
Say hi to Kosses.

62
00:11:36,259 --> 00:11:38,869
Bilecik Castle.

63
00:11:42,968 --> 00:11:44,588
Holy Jesus.

64
00:11:45,919 --> 00:11:48,039
I don't deserve you.

65
00:11:49,112 --> 00:11:55,092
I lost against the unbeliever infidels.

66
00:11:58,024 --> 00:11:59,454
Holy Jesus.

67
00:12:01,487 --> 00:12:03,017
I swear on you...

68
00:12:05,226 --> 00:12:07,326
...I am going to...

69
00:12:10,149 --> 00:12:11,709
...destroy them all.

70
00:12:15,885 --> 00:12:18,725
- Sir.
- Come.

71
00:12:20,750 --> 00:12:24,185
- Lord Nicola and Lord Kosses arrived sir.
- I'm coming.

72
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:44,240
Osman is going to Nikea.

73
00:12:44,758 --> 00:12:47,218
He'll see governor Manuel.

74
00:12:47,426 --> 00:12:49,186
We can't let this happen.

75
00:12:49,753 --> 00:12:53,423
This is going to be his last voyage.

76
00:12:54,508 --> 00:12:56,248
We'll ambush him.

77
00:12:56,248 --> 00:12:58,618
He is not taking Nikea path though.

78
00:13:00,270 --> 00:13:02,070
He took precautions.

79
00:13:03,751 --> 00:13:05,931
He'll take Kizilcahisar path.

80
00:13:07,454 --> 00:13:10,074
It's where we end him.

81
00:13:11,251 --> 00:13:14,171
So your pigeons brough news.

82
00:13:17,636 --> 00:13:20,956
I will undertake this mission.

83
00:13:22,044 --> 00:13:23,774
Does anyone object?

84
00:13:24,442 --> 00:13:27,422
You have to go with an army, Nicola.

85
00:13:28,341 --> 00:13:30,529
Take Catalans with you.

86
00:13:30,529 --> 00:13:32,479
I want to make sure he is dead.

87
00:13:34,307 --> 00:13:36,467
There's more.

88
00:13:37,630 --> 00:13:40,800
Osman is not going to take the holy relic
with him.

89
00:13:42,389 --> 00:13:44,969
He'll leave it in his tent.

90
00:13:47,366 --> 00:13:53,288
While you rip his lungs off, I'll
grab the holy relic from his tent!

91
00:13:53,288 --> 00:13:55,918
I will kill everyone who stands in my way!

92
00:13:57,664 --> 00:13:59,424
How are you going to do this?

93
00:13:59,717 --> 00:14:01,527
You'll see.

94
00:14:02,410 --> 00:14:05,210
A dead Bey, a tent without a leader...

95
00:14:05,747 --> 00:14:08,007
Finally, the end of the Turks is coming.

96
00:14:09,334 --> 00:14:14,854
We are going to attack at the right time
and right place.

97
00:14:15,227 --> 00:14:18,567
Not only Osman, Turgut should
live the same destiny!

98
00:14:21,693 --> 00:14:28,023
Nicola, Turks are dangerous when
they have a leader.

99
00:14:29,222 --> 00:14:33,142
However, Turks without a leader
are even more dangerous.

100
00:14:35,277 --> 00:14:37,097
What is your offer Kosses?

101
00:14:38,814 --> 00:14:41,864
While you are busy destroying them...

102
00:14:42,931 --> 00:14:45,191
I'll choose their leader.

103
00:14:47,266 --> 00:14:50,566
Which means I am going to
pull Turgut on our side.

104
00:15:00,198 --> 00:15:01,728
Turks...

105
00:15:02,688 --> 00:15:06,008
...follow their leaders.

106
00:15:08,966 --> 00:15:11,646
If we have Turgut...

107
00:15:13,979 --> 00:15:16,269
we have Turks as well.

108
00:15:18,440 --> 00:15:19,690
That's right.

109
00:15:27,396 --> 00:15:28,746
So we agree.

110
00:15:34,489 --> 00:15:36,149
No!

111
00:15:54,671 --> 00:15:56,221
Thank Allah

112
00:15:58,384 --> 00:16:02,394
Thank Allah, we are going to see
my child wearing this Inshallah.

113
00:16:02,751 --> 00:16:04,501
Inshallah, my Osman.

114
00:16:04,659 --> 00:16:06,209
Inshallah.

115
00:16:21,848 --> 00:16:23,988
When I go away without you...

116
00:16:24,830 --> 00:16:27,150
I always think of returning and...

117
00:16:27,640 --> 00:16:30,760
dreaming your beautiful eyes.

118
00:16:33,035 --> 00:16:37,865
I imagine you coming back and
hold onto that dream...

119
00:16:38,548 --> 00:16:40,378
and wait for you.

120
00:16:44,804 --> 00:16:51,574
Our children and our people are entrusted
to Allah first, then you.

121
00:16:53,244 --> 00:16:59,124
I'm going to protect what you entrusted me
just like I protect my love for you, my Osman.

122
00:17:00,574 --> 00:17:01,944
My Bala.

123
00:17:03,152 --> 00:17:04,521
My Bala.

124
00:17:13,451 --> 00:17:17,781
No one is leaving without taking an
oath to this agreement.

125
00:17:18,444 --> 00:17:21,515
We fell out with each other
because of Osman so many times.

126
00:17:23,252 --> 00:17:27,742
With an oath, we are going to bless
our unity that we build today.

127
00:17:29,936 --> 00:17:31,386
My friends.

128
00:17:31,808 --> 00:17:34,438
I took an oath to Caesar, Rogatus.

129
00:17:37,893 --> 00:17:41,053
I am not going to hesitate to take an oath
to Jesus.

130
00:17:41,981 --> 00:17:45,101
It's high time that we exiled Turks
from this country.

131
00:17:46,399 --> 00:17:48,429
It's time to unite.

132
00:17:52,941 --> 00:17:54,941
I swear on holy Jesus.

133
00:17:55,286 --> 00:17:57,676
I swear on holy Jesus.

134
00:17:57,985 --> 00:18:01,375
I am going to be loyal
to this unity forever.

135
00:18:01,470 --> 00:18:04,960
I am going to be loyal
to this unity forever.

136
00:18:05,172 --> 00:18:07,692
And in order to dispel Turks...

137
00:18:07,862 --> 00:18:10,542
And in order to dispel Turks...

138
00:18:10,924 --> 00:18:16,411
I am going to fight until the last
drop of my blood!

139
00:18:24,070 --> 00:18:26,830
Mother, can I come in?

140
00:18:27,183 --> 00:18:28,743
Come daughter.

141
00:18:30,889 --> 00:18:32,059
Aygül.

142
00:18:35,983 --> 00:18:37,693
Welcome daughter.

143
00:18:41,260 --> 00:18:45,170
I wanted to have your blessings before
leaving.

144
00:18:47,184 --> 00:18:49,074
Give me your blessings, mother.

145
00:18:53,119 --> 00:18:54,789
I give my blessings to you, daughter.

146
00:18:55,173 --> 00:18:57,803
Come back at once, Inshallah.

147
00:19:01,669 --> 00:19:03,139
Aygül.

148
00:19:05,918 --> 00:19:08,518
There's something else, huh?

149
00:19:09,276 --> 00:19:10,896
Come here.

150
00:19:12,869 --> 00:19:14,769
Sit down.

151
00:19:21,194 --> 00:19:25,404
Tell me.
No trouble is unsolvable with Allah.

152
00:19:27,132 --> 00:19:29,192
Show me a way, mother.

153
00:19:29,422 --> 00:19:31,602
Both my head and heart are unclear.

154
00:19:32,005 --> 00:19:34,955
What's it, inshallah?
Tell me my Aygül.

155
00:19:36,779 --> 00:19:38,399
Cerkutay.

156
00:19:40,600 --> 00:19:42,800
Cerkutay wants to marry me.

157
00:19:45,116 --> 00:19:47,136
That's not a trouble.

158
00:19:48,754 --> 00:19:52,704
Be happy, daughter.
why are you sad?

159
00:19:56,693 --> 00:20:00,113
Cerkutay is a good man.

160
00:20:02,502 --> 00:20:04,192
He is brave.

161
00:20:05,392 --> 00:20:07,292
He is merciful.

162
00:20:08,986 --> 00:20:11,946
He makes me smile when I don't.

163
00:20:13,483 --> 00:20:15,213
So?

164
00:20:16,085 --> 00:20:17,575
But...

165
00:20:21,355 --> 00:20:22,655
But...

166
00:20:25,353 --> 00:20:27,753
You know what I went through, mother.

167
00:20:29,149 --> 00:20:31,199
I cannot trust anyone.

168
00:20:31,692 --> 00:20:33,282
I am afraid.

169
00:20:36,120 --> 00:20:39,930
My father from my blood first...

170
00:20:40,715 --> 00:20:44,065
...then the betrayal of the man
that they made me marry.

171
00:20:47,666 --> 00:20:50,056
Everyone I leant on has fallen.

172
00:20:53,417 --> 00:20:56,347
I have been leaning only
on myself since then...

173
00:20:57,029 --> 00:20:58,589
so that I don't fall.

174
00:21:01,244 --> 00:21:06,504
Your tongue and heart talk differently, huh?

175
00:21:08,354 --> 00:21:10,006
Aygül.

176
00:21:11,545 --> 00:21:14,995
You like that crazy boy, don't you?

177
00:21:23,473 --> 00:21:29,133
Our ancestor said "People are diverse
just like the land"

178
00:21:30,281 --> 00:21:35,361
Why are you shutting your door to everyone
just because some people betrayed you?

179
00:21:36,481 --> 00:21:41,441
Go out now, observe anyone in the tent.
Everyone is different.

180
00:21:42,841 --> 00:21:49,901
Our prophet said "women and men are the
two parts of one whole."

181
00:21:51,630 --> 00:21:54,810
You have gone through a lot.

182
00:21:56,009 --> 00:21:58,939
You ended up with a bad guy
that didn't suit you.

183
00:21:59,770 --> 00:22:04,380
What if Allah's plan is to heal your
wound with Cerkutay...

184
00:22:04,668 --> 00:22:07,648
and complete Cerkutay with you?

185
00:22:07,866 --> 00:22:09,546
Huh?

186
00:22:10,737 --> 00:22:15,467
Allah granted that man with mercy.

187
00:22:15,982 --> 00:22:20,052
He turned his back on the cruels,
became an Alp to Osman Bey.

188
00:22:21,129 --> 00:22:24,949
Listen to me, daughter.
Think twice.

189
00:22:27,066 --> 00:22:29,336
I will think about it mother.

190
00:22:30,562 --> 00:22:33,432
I am going to think about it again.

191
00:22:35,353 --> 00:22:36,773
My beautiful daughter.

192
00:22:37,091 --> 00:22:39,101
I am glad that I have you, mother.

193
00:22:39,786 --> 00:22:41,956
I am glad that you are here.

194
00:22:42,316 --> 00:22:43,926
Always, daughter.

195
00:22:47,124 --> 00:22:48,674
Always.

196
00:22:57,939 --> 00:23:02,829
Alps that Turgut sent to follow us.

197
00:23:18,183 --> 00:23:22,993
The last face they see will be
Anselmo's face.

198
00:24:09,684 --> 00:24:11,094
Let them go.

199
00:24:16,630 --> 00:24:20,090
Let's see if they can go back to
their tent now.

200
00:25:17,956 --> 00:25:21,236
It's not enough to blind Turks, Anselmo.

201
00:25:33,009 --> 00:25:35,259
You have to kill them.

202
00:25:35,361 --> 00:25:37,321
You have to kill Turks.

203
00:25:37,494 --> 00:25:41,874
You...must...kill...kill them Anselmo!

204
00:25:56,287 --> 00:25:59,017
We are going to kill Osman, Anselmo.

205
00:25:59,695 --> 00:26:01,555
Are you ready for it?

206
00:26:02,032 --> 00:26:03,932
We are already late, Nicola.

207
00:26:03,962 --> 00:26:08,292
I swear that today is going
to their last day.

208
00:26:33,872 --> 00:26:36,572
May Allah grant you with victory.

209
00:26:36,602 --> 00:26:38,292
Thank you Bala.

210
00:26:39,243 --> 00:26:40,833
Thank you.

211
00:26:57,834 --> 00:26:59,714
Masha Allah (praise be).

212
00:27:09,990 --> 00:27:12,160
Masha Allah my son.

213
00:27:16,085 --> 00:27:17,575
Mother.

214
00:27:20,237 --> 00:27:23,597
Go well and return well, son.

215
00:27:23,717 --> 00:27:26,267
May Allah open your way.

216
00:27:26,824 --> 00:27:28,454
Amin mother.

217
00:27:29,256 --> 00:27:30,482
Amin.

218
00:27:30,482 --> 00:27:32,392
May Allah bless you Bala Hatun.

219
00:27:44,824 --> 00:27:48,344
My Bey, we brought the gifts.
We are waiting for your command.

220
00:27:48,751 --> 00:27:50,821
Ride the horses.

221
00:28:13,492 --> 00:28:14,952
Go!

222
00:28:15,118 --> 00:28:16,118
Go!

223
00:28:37,158 --> 00:28:39,998
Bilecik Castle.

224
00:28:41,281 --> 00:28:46,361
Nicola is after Osman, your guys
will infiltrate into Kayi tent.

225
00:28:47,924 --> 00:28:49,644
What a nice day.

226
00:28:51,822 --> 00:28:57,932
Rogatus, you haven't told me how
you are going to infiltrate into Kayi tent.

227
00:29:45,316 --> 00:29:47,216
Lord Rogatus.

228
00:29:47,967 --> 00:29:49,737
Lord Kosses.

229
00:29:51,695 --> 00:29:53,495
I am Julia.

230
00:29:56,447 --> 00:30:01,977
Here is the person who'll bring death
to Osman's tribe.

231
00:30:04,962 --> 00:30:06,662
Magnificus.
(Splendid)

232
00:30:06,978 --> 00:30:08,818
Class act.

233
00:30:10,225 --> 00:30:17,355
How is this beautiful angel going
to manage everything by herself, Rogatus?

234
00:30:40,836 --> 00:30:43,826
Who said I am alone, Lord Kosses?

235
00:30:44,371 --> 00:30:46,481
We are an army.

236
00:30:48,313 --> 00:30:51,193
Our name is the angels of death.

237
00:30:53,038 --> 00:30:54,918
The angels of death.

238
00:30:59,250 --> 00:31:02,450
Nice. So, how are the angels of death...

239
00:31:02,588 --> 00:31:05,848
going to infiltrate into Kayi tent?

240
00:31:06,294 --> 00:31:08,184
Dodurgalı!

241
00:31:17,848 --> 00:31:21,308
He is a Turkish merchant.

242
00:31:22,368 --> 00:31:24,998
He is going to deliver oil to Osman's tent.

243
00:31:25,498 --> 00:31:27,408
Now I understand.

244
00:31:28,027 --> 00:31:31,387
Meanwhile, our beautiful
angel will possess our relic

245
00:31:33,434 --> 00:31:37,204
By killing every Turk standing on her way.

246
00:31:49,560 --> 00:31:52,500
So, what about this one?

247
00:31:52,770 --> 00:31:54,040
He is fine.

248
00:31:55,592 --> 00:31:57,432
It's a simple poison.

249
00:31:58,683 --> 00:32:01,773
He will die if he is not treated
for a while.

250
00:32:07,507 --> 00:32:09,157
Very nice.

251
00:32:10,038 --> 00:32:11,578
Very nice.

252
00:32:11,902 --> 00:32:16,902
I want you to use this while carrying
death to Osman's tribe.

253
00:32:17,400 --> 00:32:19,200
Whatever you say.

254
00:32:59,504 --> 00:33:01,374
- Goktug!
- Yes my Bey.

255
00:33:02,159 --> 00:33:04,519
- Are the horses shoed?
- Yes my Bey.

256
00:33:09,921 --> 00:33:12,171
We'll take Kızılhisar path.

257
00:33:12,484 --> 00:33:15,414
The infidels must have heard that
we are on our way to Iznik.

258
00:33:16,726 --> 00:33:20,436
The infidels think they set up a game
but my Bey ruins them!

259
00:33:25,679 --> 00:33:28,749
Let's go!
We don't have time to waste.

260
00:33:55,253 --> 00:33:59,103
They are not aware that they are
riding their beloved horses to death!

261
00:33:59,760 --> 00:34:03,470
Not only Osman, we are going to
end them all, Anselmo!

262
00:34:05,397 --> 00:34:08,627
This land will be covered with
Turkish blood today.

263
00:34:09,574 --> 00:34:11,224
Don't doubt that.

264
00:34:14,732 --> 00:34:17,512
Come, Osman Bey.

265
00:34:18,150 --> 00:34:19,891
Come.

266
00:35:45,271 --> 00:35:46,674
Investigate.

267
00:35:46,674 --> 00:35:49,074
Yes my Bey.

268
00:36:19,043 --> 00:36:20,313
Water.

269
00:36:22,060 --> 00:36:23,560
Water.

270
00:36:24,242 --> 00:36:26,102
We'll bring now.

271
00:36:41,636 --> 00:36:43,006
Osman!

272
00:36:43,354 --> 00:36:44,824
Malhun!

273
00:36:59,047 --> 00:37:00,627
Bala.

274
00:37:02,858 --> 00:37:05,498
What's it, daughter?
Are you okay?

275
00:37:06,138 --> 00:37:07,188
I am okay.

276
00:37:07,381 --> 00:37:09,301
But I felt something bad.

277
00:37:09,902 --> 00:37:11,822
May Allah end it up well, Inshallah.

278
00:37:14,394 --> 00:37:15,394
Osman!

279
00:37:26,606 --> 00:37:28,556
He is not hungry.

280
00:37:30,314 --> 00:37:32,134
Why is he not sleeping?

281
00:37:45,784 --> 00:37:47,254
My Bey!

282
00:37:54,393 --> 00:37:55,973
My Bey!

283
00:38:06,136 --> 00:38:08,140
- Alps!
- Osman!

284
00:38:08,140 --> 00:38:09,870
Malhun.

285
00:38:29,483 --> 00:38:31,193
Attack!

286
00:38:31,193 --> 00:38:32,483
Catalans!

287
00:39:01,005 --> 00:39:02,615
Allah-u Aqbar
(Allah is the greatest)

288
00:39:48,323 --> 00:39:49,813
Osman!

289
00:39:59,184 --> 00:40:01,524
Protect my children, my Allah.

290
00:40:03,125 --> 00:40:08,375
My son sleeps well...

291
00:40:09,988 --> 00:40:15,718
He sleeps, he grows up...

292
00:40:18,504 --> 00:40:23,614
Before the birds return

293
00:40:26,973 --> 00:40:33,053
His father will come

294
00:40:42,250 --> 00:40:44,640
- Osman!
- Malhun!

295
00:41:29,943 --> 00:41:31,783
Infidel dog!

296
00:41:33,813 --> 00:41:36,013
Come to me, come!

297
00:42:29,392 --> 00:42:31,102
Finally!

298
00:42:32,248 --> 00:42:33,808
Finally!

299
00:43:07,772 --> 00:43:09,100
My Bey!

300
00:43:09,100 --> 00:43:11,520
Die already! Die already!

301
00:43:11,757 --> 00:43:13,477
Die!

302
00:44:06,602 --> 00:44:10,712
In the forest we haunt down the jackals
who set a trap on the path

303
00:44:11,238 --> 00:44:13,378
Retreat!

304
00:44:13,590 --> 00:44:16,410
Osman!
Don't let him run away!

305
00:44:16,487 --> 00:44:18,997
- Osman, are you okay?
- I am fine.

306
00:44:50,491 --> 00:44:52,271
Osman!

307
00:44:58,051 --> 00:45:00,431
Don't let him run away!
Follow him!

308
00:45:48,082 --> 00:45:49,652
Malhun.

309
00:45:52,439 --> 00:45:53,939
Let's go.

310
00:46:47,114 --> 00:46:48,714
Let's do it Malhun!

311
00:47:16,416 --> 00:47:18,196
Are you fine, brother?

312
00:47:19,685 --> 00:47:23,345
My wound is okay, Boran
but I am not okay.

313
00:47:23,456 --> 00:47:26,976
Being okay is haram until
I kill them!

314
00:47:27,734 --> 00:47:30,004
Sure brother, sure.

315
00:47:30,345 --> 00:47:32,195
We must find my Bey first.

316
00:47:32,321 --> 00:47:34,611
- Let's search now!
- Let's go!

317
00:47:46,367 --> 00:47:48,417
- My Bey!
- Cerkutay.

318
00:47:51,346 --> 00:47:52,966
Cerkutay!

319
00:47:53,159 --> 00:47:54,909
Cerkutay stop!

320
00:47:55,183 --> 00:47:58,013
Stop!
I'll bandage your wound.

321
00:48:00,083 --> 00:48:03,883
The big wound here cannot be bandaged.

322
00:48:05,326 --> 00:48:07,916
- My Bey!
- You are going to bleed to death!

323
00:48:08,036 --> 00:48:10,116
Cerkutay won't die!

324
00:48:12,401 --> 00:48:13,731
Especially...

325
00:48:16,685 --> 00:48:19,095
not before finding his Bey.

326
00:48:21,745 --> 00:48:23,545
You Allah-sent crazy!

327
00:48:34,981 --> 00:48:37,131
- My Bey!
- Cerkutay!

328
00:48:39,560 --> 00:48:41,210
Any sign?

329
00:48:41,842 --> 00:48:44,642
No.
You don't have one either I guess.

330
00:48:47,024 --> 00:48:50,674
This forest shall be my grave if I leave
without finding my Bey!

331
00:48:51,402 --> 00:48:53,802
If they did something to my Bey...

332
00:48:54,115 --> 00:48:56,815
I'll be chasing them with my
two blades!

333
00:48:56,815 --> 00:48:59,085
Don't talk nonsense, Cerkutay!

334
00:48:59,091 --> 00:49:01,471
Catalan dogs cannot hurt my Bey!

335
00:49:01,622 --> 00:49:05,442
Shut up! Malhun Hatun is with them.

336
00:49:05,948 --> 00:49:08,064
I hope we find them safe and sound.

337
00:49:08,064 --> 00:49:09,782
The forest is large!
Don't stand!

338
00:49:09,782 --> 00:49:11,784
Aygül, Aygül, stop.

339
00:49:11,784 --> 00:49:15,404
We can't split, brothers.
The infidels are everywhere.

340
00:49:15,607 --> 00:49:16,947
You are right.

341
00:49:17,019 --> 00:49:19,979
We won't stop until we find our Bey!
We'll search till dawn!

342
00:49:21,030 --> 00:49:23,920
Brothers, keep your eyes open.

343
00:49:24,017 --> 00:49:26,237
Both for our Bey and the enemy!
Let's go!

344
00:49:26,286 --> 00:49:28,156
Let's go.

345
00:50:06,339 --> 00:50:08,069
Where are you headed?

346
00:50:09,575 --> 00:50:12,565
Many will bleed today.

347
00:50:16,805 --> 00:50:19,095
You are the one to die if
someone has to.

348
00:50:20,592 --> 00:50:23,392
I have been waiting for this
moment for days, Osman.

349
00:50:44,006 --> 00:50:46,336
Come to me, Anselmo.

350
00:52:07,358 --> 00:52:09,238
Don't be afraid.

351
00:52:25,324 --> 00:52:26,944
Malhun.

352
00:52:30,629 --> 00:52:32,279
Malhun.

353
00:52:41,304 --> 00:52:43,724
Everytime I raise my sword...

354
00:52:45,046 --> 00:52:47,336
You were there.

355
00:52:50,125 --> 00:52:52,745
You killed my Alps.

356
00:52:56,412 --> 00:52:59,002
You intended to kill my unborn
child...

357
00:52:59,695 --> 00:53:01,565
and my Hatuns.

358
00:53:07,939 --> 00:53:09,739
Now...

359
00:53:11,408 --> 00:53:13,628
Your time is up.

360
00:54:35,354 --> 00:54:37,774
Find them!
Hurry!

361
00:54:42,042 --> 00:54:44,002
Let's go.

362
00:55:02,704 --> 00:55:04,154
Argos!

363
00:55:05,074 --> 00:55:07,465
You take men and keep searching back.

364
00:55:07,465 --> 00:55:12,015
Do not come without Osman!
Do not!

365
00:55:12,266 --> 00:55:15,648
Today I'll see Osman dead right here.

366
00:55:15,648 --> 00:55:18,448
Yes sir!
You two! Come with me!

367
00:55:22,636 --> 00:55:24,056
Keep on!

368
00:56:59,527 --> 00:57:01,097
How?

369
00:57:01,899 --> 00:57:03,539
How?

370
00:57:08,166 --> 00:57:12,776
How did that man manage to do this
in that situation?

371
00:57:13,081 --> 00:57:14,671
How?

372
00:57:16,519 --> 00:57:17,579
He is not dying.

373
00:57:18,183 --> 00:57:19,833
He is not dying.

374
00:57:19,950 --> 00:57:22,220
Why is that man not dying?

375
00:57:22,379 --> 00:57:25,379
Why?
He is not dying.

376
00:57:25,379 --> 00:57:27,669
That man is not dying!

377
00:57:28,514 --> 00:57:30,634
He is not dying!

378
00:57:35,616 --> 00:57:38,176
Search everywhere!
Split and search everywhere!

379
00:57:38,307 --> 00:57:41,367
Everywhere! Everywhere! Everywhere!

380
00:57:53,549 --> 00:57:55,589
Why is he not dying?

381
00:57:57,693 --> 00:58:00,103
This man is not dying!
He is not dying!

382
00:58:08,227 --> 00:58:10,507
Osman, Osman!

383
00:58:13,471 --> 00:58:15,251
Osman.

384
00:58:52,197 --> 00:58:55,177
Osman, Osman, Osman.

385
00:58:55,339 --> 00:58:57,919
Osman hold on, hold on.

386
00:58:59,682 --> 00:59:01,372
We have to go.

387
00:59:02,190 --> 00:59:03,760
Hang on!

388
00:59:04,443 --> 00:59:07,743
Osman, hang on.

389
00:59:08,389 --> 00:59:11,099
Hold onto me. Hold onto me.

390
00:59:12,193 --> 00:59:13,763
Come on.

391
00:59:24,078 --> 00:59:25,728
Somewhere...

392
00:59:26,625 --> 00:59:29,775
Somewhere like a cave...

393
00:59:30,424 --> 00:59:32,304
...we must find.

394
00:59:41,306 --> 00:59:42,816
Osman.

395
00:59:45,973 --> 00:59:47,813
Osman.

396
00:59:59,071 --> 01:00:01,831
Harmankaya Castle.

397
01:00:02,963 --> 01:00:06,103
Destroying both Osman and his tent
at the same time.

398
01:00:06,584 --> 01:00:08,924
This is going to end Turks.

399
01:00:09,936 --> 01:00:11,876
Osman will die.

400
01:00:14,781 --> 01:00:19,141
He will die but...

401
01:00:19,429 --> 01:00:22,479
I don't want to struggle with Turks
after Osman dies.

402
01:00:23,907 --> 01:00:26,947
This is where you step in, Mari.

403
01:00:27,572 --> 01:00:29,982
- Turgut.
- Turgut, ya.

404
01:00:30,539 --> 01:00:33,169
We must pull him on our side.

405
01:00:33,967 --> 01:00:35,777
How are you going to do it?

406
01:00:36,312 --> 01:00:38,362
Everyone likes power, brother.

407
01:00:38,543 --> 01:00:40,463
I'll promise him power.

408
01:00:41,704 --> 01:00:46,604
He is brave enough to replace Osman,
and as ambitious has him.

409
01:00:46,968 --> 01:00:48,998
I am sure he'll accept this.

410
01:00:50,430 --> 01:00:53,380
You'll go to Turgut first thing
in the morning.

411
01:00:55,249 --> 01:00:57,499
I trust you Mari.

412
01:00:57,969 --> 01:01:01,319
Don't worry, Turgut is in my hand.

413
01:01:03,600 --> 01:01:05,080
Nice.

414
01:01:10,940 --> 01:01:12,380
Osman.

415
01:01:13,424 --> 01:01:15,164
Okay, hold on.

416
01:01:16,089 --> 01:01:17,619
Hold on.

417
01:01:21,269 --> 01:01:23,039
Easy, Osman.

418
01:01:23,317 --> 01:01:25,273
Make a fire.

419
01:01:25,273 --> 01:01:27,973
Sit down, my Osman.

420
01:01:31,478 --> 01:01:33,378
Make a fire.

421
01:01:45,887 --> 01:01:47,707
Osman.

422
01:01:48,609 --> 01:01:50,589
Make a fire.

423
01:01:50,954 --> 01:01:52,824
Come on, make a fire.

424
01:01:52,826 --> 01:01:54,556
Hurry!

425
01:02:09,973 --> 01:02:12,173
Osman, my Osman!
I am here.

426
01:02:48,911 --> 01:02:51,391
I cannot wait, come on!

427
01:02:51,473 --> 01:02:53,103
Hurry!

428
01:02:54,876 --> 01:02:57,026
Osman, Osman.

429
01:03:00,417 --> 01:03:02,297
Hold on Osman.

430
01:03:02,986 --> 01:03:05,556
O the Healer!
O the Healer!

431
01:03:05,851 --> 01:03:07,621
O the Healer!

432
01:03:10,428 --> 01:03:12,038
Hold on my Osman!

433
01:03:25,941 --> 01:03:28,491
Okay, okay, come.

434
01:03:40,193 --> 01:03:41,773
Hold on to me.

435
01:03:42,704 --> 01:03:43,824
Hold on.

436
01:04:15,510 --> 01:04:17,640
Hold on Osman.

437
01:04:17,724 --> 01:04:19,324
Hold on.

438
01:04:19,941 --> 01:04:21,391
Wait.

439
01:04:26,726 --> 01:04:28,296
Osman.

440
01:04:30,392 --> 01:04:33,622
O the Healer! O the Healer!

441
01:04:39,182 --> 01:04:41,902
O the Healer! O the Healer!

442
01:05:11,466 --> 01:05:13,376
Allah heals.

443
01:05:18,976 --> 01:05:21,046
My Allah, give Osman more power.

444
01:05:21,462 --> 01:05:23,852
Give Osman more power.

445
01:05:31,832 --> 01:05:36,712
Polytheists set many traps for
Allah's messenger.

446
01:05:37,360 --> 01:05:41,580
Our prophet firstly took caution...

447
01:05:41,745 --> 01:05:45,205
then trusted in Allah.

448
01:05:46,579 --> 01:05:49,979
In Battle of the Trench,
the trenches...

449
01:05:50,488 --> 01:05:52,088
were precaution.

450
01:05:53,402 --> 01:05:58,332
When the polytheists attempted
to take his sacred life...

451
01:05:58,681 --> 01:06:05,541
taking the hard road instead of
the short road...

452
01:06:05,541 --> 01:06:08,536
and taking shelter in...

453
01:06:08,536 --> 01:06:12,476
Sevr Cave with his friend
Hz.Ebubakir...

454
01:06:13,052 --> 01:06:15,152
was a precaution.

455
01:06:16,119 --> 01:06:21,099
But despite all these precautions...

456
01:06:21,563 --> 01:06:25,533
the most talented trackers
of the polytheists...

457
01:06:25,759 --> 01:06:29,679
came all the way to the
entrance of that cave.

458
01:06:31,463 --> 01:06:34,223
And even a crumble of fear...

459
01:06:35,246 --> 01:06:39,146
wasn't present in our prophet's heart.

460
01:06:40,758 --> 01:06:45,188
Because in the verse that came for
him, Allah said...

461
01:06:45,437 --> 01:06:48,850
''and Allah too plans...

462
01:06:48,850 --> 01:06:52,020
but the best of planners is Allah.''

463
01:06:53,886 --> 01:06:57,096
We believe that...

464
01:06:57,684 --> 01:07:03,224
the best of planners is Allah.

465
01:07:04,656 --> 01:07:09,146
And he is always with
his subjects.

466
01:07:11,381 --> 01:07:17,201
In this world, neither the tyrants nor
tyranny will end.

467
01:07:18,882 --> 01:07:24,322
When Muslims take precautions
and trust in Allah...

468
01:07:25,405 --> 01:07:29,875
all plans made by the tyrants can
be deflected.

469
01:07:45,059 --> 01:07:46,739
My Orhan.

470
01:07:47,351 --> 01:07:49,011
My son.

471
01:07:50,392 --> 01:07:51,932
Osman!

472
01:07:53,815 --> 01:07:55,685
You are alright.
Thank Allah.

473
01:07:58,500 --> 01:08:00,350
I'm fine.

474
01:08:00,398 --> 01:08:02,018
I'm fine.

475
01:08:02,882 --> 01:08:04,972
What about you?

476
01:08:05,102 --> 01:08:07,697
I'm fine.
As long as you are good...

477
01:08:07,697 --> 01:08:09,857
nothing will happen to me.

478
01:08:13,706 --> 01:08:15,736
My Orhan.

479
01:08:16,194 --> 01:08:17,899
You are wounded.

480
01:08:17,899 --> 01:08:20,060
It's not important, Osman.

481
01:08:23,118 --> 01:08:24,979
Malhun...

482
01:08:28,058 --> 01:08:29,881
We need to burn it.

483
01:08:29,881 --> 01:08:31,886
I'll do it.
Just get some rest.

484
01:08:31,886 --> 01:08:33,917
We need to burn it.

485
01:08:33,917 --> 01:08:35,747
Come on.

486
01:08:36,243 --> 01:08:38,913
Alright. Slowly.

487
01:08:43,419 --> 01:08:45,439
Slowly. Slowly.

488
01:08:46,604 --> 01:08:48,184
Don't tire yourself.

489
01:08:58,808 --> 01:09:01,138
With the name of Allah.

490
01:09:13,161 --> 01:09:15,461
My brave wife.

491
01:09:42,285 --> 01:09:44,095
Come.

492
01:09:54,896 --> 01:09:56,756
Osman.

493
01:09:58,042 --> 01:10:00,372
As long as I have you...

494
01:10:00,372 --> 01:10:03,242
nothing can take me down.

495
01:10:06,922 --> 01:10:09,052
True.

496
01:10:13,966 --> 01:10:15,916
Thank you.

497
01:10:19,054 --> 01:10:20,844
Thank you.

498
01:10:29,367 --> 01:10:31,127
Always...

499
01:10:32,770 --> 01:10:35,830
you stand behind me like a mountain.

500
01:10:37,002 --> 01:10:39,592
I never get down.

501
01:10:40,352 --> 01:10:42,342
Never.

502
01:10:43,647 --> 01:10:46,657
You lighten up the darkness.

503
01:10:48,412 --> 01:10:50,192
You do.

504
01:10:55,365 --> 01:10:57,405
True.

505
01:10:59,166 --> 01:11:01,376
True.

506
01:11:02,788 --> 01:11:05,778
With Allah's help, we'll
get out of here too.

507
01:11:06,751 --> 01:11:09,111
We will find our alps.

508
01:11:12,569 --> 01:11:15,979
The heathens who try to stop us...

509
01:11:17,449 --> 01:11:19,709
will lose their lives.

510
01:11:20,439 --> 01:11:23,339
We won't let them run away.

511
01:11:24,231 --> 01:11:26,231
We will, Osman.

512
01:11:26,760 --> 01:11:28,480
Inshallah.

513
01:11:34,504 --> 01:11:36,624
Bilecik Castle

514
01:11:38,764 --> 01:11:43,604
Ever since the day Turks killed me
parents, I waited for this day, Rogatus.

515
01:11:45,513 --> 01:11:49,333
I didn't spend a day without thinking
about killing them.

516
01:11:50,804 --> 01:11:53,579
That's why I trained the
Death Angels.

517
01:11:53,579 --> 01:11:56,579
They all were born to kill.

518
01:11:56,936 --> 01:11:58,656
I know, Julia.

519
01:12:00,310 --> 01:12:04,230
You are an amazing warrior and
so are your soldiers.

520
01:12:05,685 --> 01:12:09,305
But your greatest weapon is
your revenge.

521
01:12:10,387 --> 01:12:13,667
My family died to keep the
Turks out of these lands.

522
01:12:14,783 --> 01:12:18,313
I will finish what they left
unfinished.

523
01:12:18,963 --> 01:12:21,683
I will take them out of these lands.

524
01:12:22,009 --> 01:12:23,929
Show me a target.

525
01:12:26,565 --> 01:12:28,915
I wouldn't find anyone better for
this job.

526
01:12:31,983 --> 01:12:35,093
Soon, you will get your revenge, Julia.

527
01:12:50,192 --> 01:12:52,252
My Allah.

528
01:12:54,473 --> 01:12:57,453
I take shelter under you against
every trouble.

529
01:12:58,303 --> 01:13:02,853
You found a cure for Job's
merciless nuisance.

530
01:13:04,147 --> 01:13:08,277
You let Jonah live in a fish's belly.

531
01:13:09,108 --> 01:13:12,468
You took Joseph out of that well.

532
01:13:14,271 --> 01:13:20,081
You protected our holy and sacred prophet
Muhammed against the polytheists.

533
01:13:21,753 --> 01:13:28,673
In the cave he hid in, you protected him
with a bird's egg and a spider web.

534
01:13:29,635 --> 01:13:32,205
O' my merciful Allah!

535
01:13:32,558 --> 01:13:36,278
For your prophets and saints....

536
01:13:36,640 --> 01:13:41,100
help us. Destine us to find my
alps safe and sound.

537
01:13:41,545 --> 01:13:46,565
Destine us to take the revenge
of our martyrs.

538
01:13:47,706 --> 01:13:51,006
We have no other door to knock.

539
01:13:51,360 --> 01:13:54,940
Don't return us empty-handed, my Allah!

540
01:13:59,225 --> 01:14:01,125
Amin, my Allah.

541
01:14:03,333 --> 01:14:05,083
Amin.

542
01:14:21,666 --> 01:14:24,136
Bilecik Castle

543
01:15:34,336 --> 01:15:40,886
Even if the earth goes down,
justice will prevail.

544
01:16:00,019 --> 01:16:01,759
Turks.

545
01:16:02,216 --> 01:16:05,590
I will end you with my own hands.

546
01:16:13,998 --> 01:16:17,298
You took my family from me.

547
01:16:17,907 --> 01:16:21,847
I won't die before taking everything
from you.

548
01:16:59,407 --> 01:17:02,291
You will die, Turks!

549
01:17:02,291 --> 01:17:04,631
You all will die!

550
01:17:04,903 --> 01:17:07,203
And it will be my poison that caused it.

551
01:17:13,267 --> 01:17:18,317
Osman Bey said that he will buy the
rest of the goods and compensate.

552
01:17:19,154 --> 01:17:21,424
The first group will come today,
inshallah.

553
01:17:23,695 --> 01:17:27,305
Thank Allah, Osman Bey is the hope
of all Turkmens.

554
01:17:29,036 --> 01:17:32,266
They might want to take advantage
from Osman Bey's absence.

555
01:17:32,943 --> 01:17:35,243
We don't have just one enemy.

556
01:17:36,027 --> 01:17:38,953
Don't drop your guard, Gündüz.

557
01:17:38,953 --> 01:17:42,993
Mother, don't worry.
Alps will be careful.

558
01:17:45,009 --> 01:17:47,139
We are here too.

559
01:17:47,783 --> 01:17:49,903
Be at ease.

560
01:18:26,158 --> 01:18:28,508
No one will survive!

561
01:18:57,215 --> 01:18:59,275
I'm working for Rogatus, you know it.

562
01:19:00,341 --> 01:19:03,441
You will live because you
will help us.

563
01:19:07,941 --> 01:19:10,741
Rogatus and Kosses are waiting for us.
Hurry!

564
01:19:19,706 --> 01:19:21,176
Come on!

565
01:19:56,459 --> 01:19:57,979
Slowly.

566
01:20:00,785 --> 01:20:02,175
Slowly.

567
01:20:03,034 --> 01:20:04,614
Slowly.

568
01:20:23,567 --> 01:20:26,687
Despite all the caution,
they ambushed us!

569
01:20:26,760 --> 01:20:29,170
There is a traitor in the tribe.

570
01:20:29,796 --> 01:20:32,056
We need to return to the tribe
at once then!

571
01:20:32,930 --> 01:20:34,710
No.

572
01:20:34,788 --> 01:20:36,948
The tribe has many protectors.

573
01:20:37,666 --> 01:20:39,486
We will move forward.

574
01:20:40,535 --> 01:20:44,965
But we need to find the alps first.

575
01:20:48,907 --> 01:20:52,297
Like this, my bey? You are on your feet
but you aren't alright.

576
01:20:53,918 --> 01:20:56,188
I won't return empty-handed.

577
01:20:57,488 --> 01:20:59,818
The people await good news.

578
01:21:00,664 --> 01:21:03,664
Alright but which way will we
go, my bey?

579
01:21:03,790 --> 01:21:05,740
It's a huge forest!

580
01:21:06,964 --> 01:21:08,574
We'll find it, Malhun.

581
01:21:09,635 --> 01:21:11,235
We'll find it.

582
01:21:13,436 --> 01:21:14,966
Cerkutay.

583
01:21:16,125 --> 01:21:18,475
My lion must've thought something.

584
01:21:19,426 --> 01:21:21,086
Come on.

585
01:21:53,530 --> 01:21:56,040
Brother. Did you find a track?

586
01:22:03,034 --> 01:22:04,184
No.

587
01:22:08,129 --> 01:22:10,619
No trace.

588
01:22:17,510 --> 01:22:19,900
No trace.

589
01:22:25,643 --> 01:22:29,053
If we can't find our bey.

590
01:22:31,286 --> 01:22:33,376
Let him find us, brothers.

591
01:24:30,968 --> 01:24:32,588
Come on!

592
01:24:33,307 --> 01:24:35,377
My crazy brother.

593
01:24:57,016 --> 01:24:58,746
Well done, Rogatus.

594
01:24:58,957 --> 01:25:01,997
Your carpenters did a really good job.

595
01:25:03,048 --> 01:25:09,068
Now the only thing to do is take over
those carts to enter Kayı Tribe.

596
01:25:10,146 --> 01:25:14,376
And that was your pretty angel's task.
Do you think they did it?

597
01:25:16,029 --> 01:25:20,339
You shouldn't be doubting after
yesterday's show, Kosses.

598
01:25:21,115 --> 01:25:24,165
And they should've been here, Rogatus.

599
01:25:31,329 --> 01:25:33,029
Here they are.

600
01:25:40,337 --> 01:25:42,757
Are you sure it's them, Rogatus?

601
01:25:46,538 --> 01:25:48,648
Aren't they Turkmens?

602
01:26:13,761 --> 01:26:15,661
Dear lords.

603
01:26:15,962 --> 01:26:18,092
We are ready to enter the tribe.

604
01:26:18,355 --> 01:26:19,975
What about poison?

605
01:26:20,187 --> 01:26:22,217
It's ready, as you ordered.

606
01:26:22,594 --> 01:26:25,254
It will be the end of every Turk
that stands in my way.

607
01:26:30,117 --> 01:26:33,047
As I see, you also completed
your preperations.

608
01:26:33,446 --> 01:26:35,386
Of course.

609
01:26:35,762 --> 01:26:38,062
Lestor will accompany you.

610
01:26:40,502 --> 01:26:47,612
So, only thing left to do is to become
the nightmare of Osman's tribe.

611
01:27:37,251 --> 01:27:40,531
-Turgut Bey.
-Mari. What are you doing here?

612
01:27:42,980 --> 01:27:45,740
I'm here by my brother Michael Kosses's
orders.

613
01:27:46,797 --> 01:27:48,727
What does your brother want?

614
01:27:48,833 --> 01:27:51,263
Did he send you instead of
coming here?

615
01:27:52,091 --> 01:27:54,231
Is he that afraid?

616
01:27:54,722 --> 01:27:57,562
Michael Kosses isn't afraid of anyone,
Turgut Bey.

617
01:28:01,476 --> 01:28:03,966
And about my visitation.

618
01:28:26,105 --> 01:28:27,855
Are you alright, Osman?

619
01:28:29,124 --> 01:28:30,974
I'm fine.

620
01:28:31,007 --> 01:28:33,027
I'm fine.

621
01:28:50,343 --> 01:28:52,023
Alps!

622
01:28:53,128 --> 01:28:54,698
Alps!

623
01:28:56,315 --> 01:28:58,665
Alps left a track.

624
01:29:01,490 --> 01:29:04,310
They are alive, Malhun!
They are alive.

625
01:29:06,088 --> 01:29:08,728
We are getting closer, inshallah.

626
01:29:14,741 --> 01:29:16,521
Mashallah to my lions.

627
01:29:19,404 --> 01:29:21,054
Mashallah.

628
01:29:21,460 --> 01:29:22,980
Come on.

629
01:29:25,815 --> 01:29:29,135
I didn't realize it when I first came
here. Your tribe is small.

630
01:29:32,873 --> 01:29:34,233
It is.

631
01:29:35,663 --> 01:29:40,193
Osman Bey's tribe is magnificent.
It is more ordinate compared to yours.

632
01:29:41,377 --> 01:29:43,577
Oh, you Byzantines...

633
01:29:45,465 --> 01:29:47,575
Come to the point, Mari.

634
01:29:47,790 --> 01:29:49,700
Why are you here?

635
01:29:50,683 --> 01:29:56,343
We want to replace this bloody hostility
with an agreement that pleases both sides.

636
01:29:57,875 --> 01:30:00,805
My brother Michael Kosses
wants to do trade with you.

637
01:30:01,129 --> 01:30:05,009
So, both you and your small tribe
will win.

638
01:30:08,339 --> 01:30:09,979
After all the blood...

639
01:30:10,883 --> 01:30:12,863
he wants to be our friend?

640
01:30:15,478 --> 01:30:20,208
I advice you to forget the past and
start again stronger, Turgut Bey.

641
01:30:20,580 --> 01:30:24,560
What you call the past and tell me to
forget are my martyr alps.

642
01:30:25,316 --> 01:30:26,826
I won't forget it.

643
01:30:37,702 --> 01:30:39,962
But the condition of my tribe is
apparent.

644
01:30:40,537 --> 01:30:43,067
Remembering it doesn't stop
me from doing trade.

645
01:30:45,171 --> 01:30:48,351
For their well-being, I will
consider it.

646
01:30:49,868 --> 01:30:53,858
I'm guessing that you are a smart man.
I'm sure that you'll make the right call.

647
01:30:55,996 --> 01:30:59,186
But know it, my conditions
will be heavy.

648
01:31:00,000 --> 01:31:02,390
Let's talk about them when you
make your decision.

649
01:31:04,231 --> 01:31:06,651
I'll be waiting.

650
01:31:09,396 --> 01:31:11,306
Now, if you allow me.

651
01:31:25,675 --> 01:31:27,365
Turgut Bey.

652
01:31:31,602 --> 01:31:34,062
-Yes.
-I almost forgot.

653
01:31:36,810 --> 01:31:38,420
This is for you.

654
01:31:42,811 --> 01:31:44,401
Please.

655
01:31:45,285 --> 01:31:48,125
I thought it would fit a bey like you.

656
01:32:05,102 --> 01:32:06,602
Thank you, Mari.

657
01:32:08,138 --> 01:32:09,148
You...

658
01:32:10,695 --> 01:32:14,485
don't look like a man to stay
under someone else's shadow...

659
01:32:15,210 --> 01:32:16,430
Turgut Bey.

660
01:33:14,788 --> 01:33:16,378
What does she want, my bey?

661
01:33:17,666 --> 01:33:19,736
Kosses wants to trade.

662
01:33:20,281 --> 01:33:23,181
What are you saying, my bey?
Working with the heathens?

663
01:33:24,254 --> 01:33:26,734
Osman Bey has been doing politics
for so long.

664
01:33:27,449 --> 01:33:29,389
Why shouldn't we?

665
01:33:38,522 --> 01:33:40,122
My bey...

666
01:33:41,171 --> 01:33:42,511
My bey...

667
01:33:45,742 --> 01:33:48,182
Where are you, my bey?
Where are you?

668
01:34:02,322 --> 01:34:04,702
Split out, brothers!

669
01:34:04,716 --> 01:34:06,456
Come on!

670
01:34:44,974 --> 01:34:46,944
My bey!

671
01:34:49,350 --> 01:34:51,310
Thank Allah!

672
01:34:51,357 --> 01:34:53,254
-My bey!
-My bey!

673
01:34:53,254 --> 01:34:54,694
Thank Allah!

674
01:34:54,739 --> 01:34:56,840
-My bey!
-Alps!

675
01:34:56,840 --> 01:34:59,340
My bey!
My bey!

676
01:34:59,493 --> 01:35:00,683
My bey!

677
01:35:02,257 --> 01:35:03,797
My bey!

678
01:35:06,076 --> 01:35:07,816
My bey, thank Allah!

679
01:35:07,816 --> 01:35:09,836
Are you alright?

680
01:35:11,601 --> 01:35:13,231
Thank Allah!

681
01:35:14,234 --> 01:35:16,154
Are you alright, my bey?

682
01:35:16,973 --> 01:35:18,413
I'm alright.

683
01:35:18,870 --> 01:35:20,960
Thank Allah for this.

684
01:35:21,313 --> 01:35:23,063
Are you alright?

685
01:35:23,360 --> 01:35:26,340
As long as you are well, nothing can
happen to us, my bey.

686
01:35:27,942 --> 01:35:31,442
I should've known that they can't do
anything to you, my bey.

687
01:35:34,120 --> 01:35:35,890
-Aygül.
-My bey.

688
01:35:39,276 --> 01:35:42,566
-Malhun Hatun, are you alright?
-I'm good, Göktuğ.

689
01:35:44,614 --> 01:35:47,834
Who knows how you slaughtered that
dog Anselmo.

690
01:35:53,969 --> 01:35:55,809
Where is Gencebey?

691
01:35:55,838 --> 01:35:57,958
He is waiting for us at the horses.

692
01:36:01,489 --> 01:36:04,699
But my bey, you have many wounds.
Are you alright?

693
01:36:06,321 --> 01:36:08,131
Yeah.

694
01:36:08,737 --> 01:36:10,067
I'm alright.

695
01:36:13,244 --> 01:36:14,944
I'm alright.

696
01:36:15,600 --> 01:36:20,380
The swords they swing at us are
destined to go blunt.

697
01:36:21,667 --> 01:36:23,417
Thank Allah, we are alright.

698
01:36:24,479 --> 01:36:26,369
Mashallah, my bey.

699
01:36:27,049 --> 01:36:30,539
Then, let's go to the horses.

700
01:36:30,659 --> 01:36:32,119
Alright, my bey.

701
01:36:59,310 --> 01:37:02,450
-Let's search it well, brother.
-Alright, brother.

702
01:37:10,767 --> 01:37:12,817
No offence, brother.

703
01:37:42,957 --> 01:37:44,487
Let me.

704
01:38:37,271 --> 01:38:40,131
Brother. Get down.

705
01:39:17,522 --> 01:39:19,422
Brother.

706
01:39:20,160 --> 01:39:22,480
Tie them well next time.

707
01:39:23,379 --> 01:39:25,619
They were going to be spilled and wasted.

708
01:39:30,233 --> 01:39:31,873
Alright.

709
01:39:32,615 --> 01:39:34,035
Go on.

710
01:39:34,385 --> 01:39:35,955
Go on!

711
01:39:45,262 --> 01:39:47,212
Go on.

712
01:39:58,704 --> 01:40:00,244
Alps!

713
01:40:00,244 --> 01:40:04,014
Hold on! You are riding the wrong way.

714
01:40:08,221 --> 01:40:10,561
We are going to İznik.

715
01:40:15,450 --> 01:40:22,150
We won't sheath our swords until
we reach the destination.

716
01:40:23,808 --> 01:40:25,848
As you order, my bey.

717
01:40:27,777 --> 01:40:29,847
Come on.

718
01:40:59,250 --> 01:41:02,196
Mashallah, he is appetent.

719
01:41:02,196 --> 01:41:04,886
Mashallah to my lion.

720
01:41:05,174 --> 01:41:06,684
My Orhan!

721
01:41:14,474 --> 01:41:15,894
Bala?

722
01:41:18,421 --> 01:41:20,081
Bala?

723
01:41:44,864 --> 01:41:46,224
Bala?

724
01:41:49,706 --> 01:41:52,806
You are thinking about Osman Bey,
don't you?

725
01:41:58,691 --> 01:42:00,901
I feel suffocated.

726
01:42:01,223 --> 01:42:03,563
Whatever I did wasn't enough to
let it go.

727
01:42:06,162 --> 01:42:08,722
Think well so that all can be well.

728
01:42:11,767 --> 01:42:14,707
Come on, don't let Orhan get cold.

729
01:42:15,712 --> 01:42:17,502
Come on, Bala.

730
01:42:43,273 --> 01:42:46,183
Tell me, where is this oil from?

731
01:42:46,288 --> 01:42:48,378
-It's from Karailyas.
-Is that so?

732
01:42:48,819 --> 01:42:51,797
I know their oil well.

733
01:42:51,797 --> 01:42:53,937
It's really good.

734
01:43:25,277 --> 01:43:30,037
What is this? Huh? It's nothing
like their oil?

735
01:43:34,471 --> 01:43:37,891
Crops weren't good this year, I see?

736
01:43:38,972 --> 01:43:42,652
Selcan Hatun, not all can be the same.
This is how it is this year.

737
01:43:55,792 --> 01:43:59,982
Alright then. Price it accordingly.

738
01:44:10,567 --> 01:44:12,747
-Good day.
-Thank you.

739
01:44:26,780 --> 01:44:28,920
I was so close.

740
01:44:29,074 --> 01:44:31,989
I was so close, he was in my hands!

741
01:44:31,989 --> 01:44:33,919
He was in my hands!

742
01:44:35,251 --> 01:44:39,701
But then again, again, again
he ran away!

743
01:44:44,530 --> 01:44:46,090
Osman...

744
01:44:48,561 --> 01:44:54,091
He was in my hands! If he is in your
hands, you squeeze I'm like a fly!

745
01:44:54,412 --> 01:44:56,322
Like a fly!

746
01:45:03,933 --> 01:45:07,003
Where will you run, Osman Bey?
Where?

747
01:45:08,231 --> 01:45:10,201
Where?

748
01:45:12,971 --> 01:45:15,311
This is my land!

749
01:45:15,932 --> 01:45:17,902
This is my mountain!

750
01:45:18,090 --> 01:45:20,230
This is my city!

751
01:45:22,655 --> 01:45:25,355
These castles are my castles!

752
01:45:25,602 --> 01:45:29,252
These cities are mine!

753
01:45:30,589 --> 01:45:32,719
I'm Ceaser's son!

754
01:45:32,905 --> 01:45:34,775
Aya Nikola!

755
01:45:42,872 --> 01:45:46,192
And you are mine too, Osman Bey.

756
01:45:46,298 --> 01:45:48,468
You are mine!

757
01:45:53,832 --> 01:45:56,082
Do you know what I will do to you?

758
01:45:56,217 --> 01:46:01,827
I will cut off your hands, your feet...

759
01:46:02,970 --> 01:46:05,710
your fingers...

760
01:46:06,262 --> 01:46:09,852
I'll put you in a cage with your
beloved animals...

761
01:46:10,012 --> 01:46:11,902
wolves and jackals.

762
01:46:12,113 --> 01:46:16,793
I'll make them eat you bit by bit.

763
01:46:33,392 --> 01:46:37,792
But this would be a weak ending for you.

764
01:46:38,448 --> 01:46:41,628
It would be a weak ending for you.

765
01:46:41,964 --> 01:46:43,904
Do you know what I will do to you?

766
01:46:44,162 --> 01:46:48,002
I will hold you on your skull...

767
01:46:50,246 --> 01:46:52,746
and put you on the back of my horse.

768
01:46:53,526 --> 01:46:56,656
I'll walk you around all the Turkmen
tribes.

769
01:46:56,780 --> 01:46:59,470
I'll tell them to look!

770
01:47:00,607 --> 01:47:03,967
Look, look!

771
01:47:04,651 --> 01:47:08,471
Here's the head of the one who
stood up against Aya Nikola!

772
01:47:21,746 --> 01:47:23,716
Osman Bey!

773
01:47:24,521 --> 01:47:26,831
This is your blood!

774
01:47:26,916 --> 01:47:31,766
Osman Bey, I will make you choke blood!

775
01:47:35,179 --> 01:47:39,319
Whenever someone of your lineage
thinks of rebellion...

776
01:47:39,600 --> 01:47:43,360
someone of my lineage will...

777
01:47:44,374 --> 01:47:46,754
smash his head like this.

778
01:47:58,747 --> 01:47:59,957
Don't...

779
01:48:01,412 --> 01:48:05,152
don't think that you won
this war.

780
01:48:05,952 --> 01:48:07,872
Don't!

781
01:48:09,016 --> 01:48:11,956
Don't think that you've beaten me!

782
01:48:12,849 --> 01:48:14,429
Don't!

783
01:48:15,353 --> 01:48:16,933
This war...

784
01:48:19,547 --> 01:48:22,377
will be over tonight, Osman Bey.

785
01:48:23,038 --> 01:48:24,838
Tonight.

786
01:48:30,258 --> 01:48:32,708
You get it, Argos?

787
01:48:34,625 --> 01:48:36,365
I get it, sir.

788
01:48:38,248 --> 01:48:41,018
We are going to Harmankaya.

789
01:48:52,449 --> 01:48:54,739
İznik Castle

790
01:49:11,815 --> 01:49:15,575
Welcome, Saguros. What news did
you bring from Constantinople?

791
01:49:15,991 --> 01:49:18,901
I have great news, Manuel.

792
01:49:19,159 --> 01:49:23,209
The emperor congratulates you
for your services.

793
01:49:25,608 --> 01:49:28,448
Now, you need to rest.

794
01:49:31,323 --> 01:49:33,173
Forever.

795
01:49:35,307 --> 01:49:38,007
Will you overthrow me in front of
my loyal soldiers?

796
01:49:39,053 --> 01:49:43,863
In these lands, the emperor always
has the last word.

797
01:49:48,128 --> 01:49:51,768
Soldiers, help Governor Saguros leave.

798
01:50:03,185 --> 01:50:04,885
Soldiers!

799
01:50:07,228 --> 01:50:11,338
Not only your loyal soldiers, Manuel.

800
01:50:14,006 --> 01:50:18,736
Everyone in your city is under my
command now.

801
01:50:25,067 --> 01:50:26,917
You were my friend.

802
01:50:27,155 --> 01:50:31,635
Friendship. Friendship surrenders
to ambition.

803
01:50:33,544 --> 01:50:38,394
You shouldn't have put your eyes
on the emperor's throne.

804
01:50:38,440 --> 01:50:42,960
This isn't true. You did it.
You deceived the emperor!

805
01:50:43,361 --> 01:50:46,071
It's what the emperor believes.

806
01:50:56,497 --> 01:50:58,576
Harmankaya Castle

807
01:50:58,576 --> 01:51:03,136
I'm grateful that you forgot all the
trouble you had and came here.

808
01:51:03,207 --> 01:51:05,037
Turgut Bey.

809
01:51:07,915 --> 01:51:10,495
Nothing is forgotten, Kosses.

810
01:51:12,708 --> 01:51:13,868
Mari knows.

811
01:51:15,745 --> 01:51:18,175
I'm doing it for my tribe's well-being.

812
01:51:19,618 --> 01:51:21,798
And for all the Turkmens.

813
01:51:23,107 --> 01:51:27,007
You will be facing us when you
agree with us.

814
01:51:27,007 --> 01:51:31,127
When was Osman Bey with me that
I should fear that?

815
01:51:31,145 --> 01:51:35,735
From now, you are responsible for our
caravans' security.

816
01:51:36,262 --> 01:51:40,722
They'll pass through your lands and
they'll be under your responsibiilty.

817
01:51:41,576 --> 01:51:46,846
Of course, since we are in a tough
the situation, we'll be generous.

818
01:51:48,484 --> 01:51:53,204
The health of our agreement depends
on how generous you are, Kosses.

819
01:51:56,608 --> 01:51:59,488
For every caravan that reaches its
destination safely.

820
01:52:01,592 --> 01:52:05,042
You will get half of what
we earn.

821
01:52:09,002 --> 01:52:11,152
A reasonable offer.

822
01:52:11,854 --> 01:52:13,974
I wouldn't accept any less.

823
01:52:16,745 --> 01:52:19,085
I take this as a yes.

824
01:52:20,709 --> 01:52:23,159
We'll get stronger together.

825
01:52:23,970 --> 01:52:26,090
I'm glad that we have an agreement.

826
01:52:26,753 --> 01:52:29,843
If you stand with me, I'm a really
nice guy, Kosses.

827
01:52:31,415 --> 01:52:33,945
As long as you don't face me.

828
01:52:35,412 --> 01:52:38,442
Then, let it be good for everyone.

829
01:52:42,432 --> 01:52:43,992
I hope so.

830
01:53:29,718 --> 01:53:31,158
Nikola.

831
01:53:57,435 --> 01:53:59,985
İznik Castle

832
01:54:48,367 --> 01:54:50,697
Welcome, Osman Bey.

833
01:54:50,895 --> 01:54:53,455
I knew you were coming.

834
01:55:00,499 --> 01:55:02,149
Thank you.

835
01:55:03,649 --> 01:55:05,599
Thank you, but...

836
01:55:05,989 --> 01:55:08,519
I thought we were going to see
Governor Manuel.

837
01:55:09,200 --> 01:55:12,130
The Emperor resigned him.

838
01:55:14,874 --> 01:55:17,284
My name is Saguros.

839
01:55:17,648 --> 01:55:19,968
I'm the new governor of Nikea.

840
01:55:20,687 --> 01:55:21,767
So...

841
01:55:28,304 --> 01:55:31,214
what happened to you?

842
01:55:44,652 --> 01:55:47,192
They tried to stop us.

843
01:55:48,230 --> 01:55:52,850
But we let them know that
we can't be stopped.

844
01:55:54,546 --> 01:55:57,606
Catalonians and Lord Nikola...

845
01:55:59,583 --> 01:56:01,883
they ambushed us.

846
01:56:02,245 --> 01:56:05,195
Even though they knew that you were
coming to Nikea?

847
01:56:05,952 --> 01:56:08,082
What insolence is this?

848
01:56:08,540 --> 01:56:11,260
The hostility of the lords
isn't a secret.

849
01:56:12,307 --> 01:56:17,847
But assuring the security of the roads
is your job.

850
01:56:22,403 --> 01:56:27,983
Fortunately, they made a mistake
by facing us.

851
01:56:29,349 --> 01:56:31,659
We slaughtered all the Catalonians.

852
01:56:38,494 --> 01:56:40,494
Now, your roads are safe.

853
01:56:42,955 --> 01:56:48,445
I think you didn't come here to clean
the roads of Nikea.

854
01:56:52,796 --> 01:56:56,146
Since Manuel and the lords
broke the agreement...

855
01:56:56,564 --> 01:56:58,424
I'm not letting...

856
01:57:02,128 --> 01:57:05,138
a single caravan enter your lands.

857
01:57:06,075 --> 01:57:11,445
When I opened the city treasury,
I saw that it was empty.

858
01:57:12,756 --> 01:57:17,876
He spent everything he has to
feed his people.

859
01:57:20,589 --> 01:57:22,939
You must know it well...

860
01:57:23,418 --> 01:57:25,598
that you should stand with me...

861
01:57:26,219 --> 01:57:28,759
not against me.

862
01:57:29,002 --> 01:57:33,102
Don't. Don't.

863
01:57:34,130 --> 01:57:36,940
Don't make the same mistakes
with Manuel.

864
01:57:39,140 --> 01:57:41,190
Go on, Osman Bey.

865
01:57:41,607 --> 01:57:46,437
Someone who just got to their position
should please the folk.

866
01:57:50,358 --> 01:57:55,168
Otherwise, his reign won't last long.

867
01:57:56,856 --> 01:57:59,226
Are you threatening me?

868
01:58:03,561 --> 01:58:05,511
I'm saying the truth.

869
01:58:09,452 --> 01:58:11,822
The surety of your position...

870
01:58:11,986 --> 01:58:14,516
depends on the trade you will
do with me.

871
01:58:14,945 --> 01:58:18,765
Otherwise, I won't stop raiding
your caravans.

872
01:58:19,794 --> 01:58:23,154
War is a wedding for the Turks!

873
01:58:24,507 --> 01:58:27,587
Speaking this boldly...

874
01:58:28,456 --> 01:58:31,206
in my castle full of my soldiers...

875
01:58:34,980 --> 01:58:39,430
And also, you have your wife
with you.

876
01:58:40,893 --> 01:58:44,063
We say that war is a wedding
for the Turks.

877
01:58:44,114 --> 01:58:45,914
Not for the men.

878
01:58:50,064 --> 01:58:54,224
Women are no different than men.
We aren't afraid.

879
01:59:00,626 --> 01:59:02,846
You are right.

880
01:59:08,028 --> 01:59:11,498
So, what's your offer?

881
01:59:23,251 --> 01:59:25,611
Whatever you get from...

882
01:59:26,428 --> 01:59:31,198
your trade with the lords,
I'll give you double.

883
01:59:34,450 --> 01:59:37,260
We've come from a tough road.

884
01:59:39,621 --> 01:59:42,211
All our gifts are wasted.

885
01:59:44,039 --> 01:59:45,569
For this reason.

886
02:00:01,144 --> 02:00:04,094
I want to give you this as a token.

887
02:00:42,489 --> 02:00:47,129
Kayı Tribe will provide all the needs
of İznik.

888
02:00:48,625 --> 02:00:50,975
I will personally protect the caravans.

889
02:00:54,509 --> 02:00:56,739
Where the Turks exist...

890
02:00:58,285 --> 02:01:01,105
there is no other way than
making an agreement.

891
02:01:04,116 --> 02:01:05,656
Know it.

892
02:01:20,541 --> 02:01:26,151
Call the clerk. We'll make an agreement
with Osman Bey.

893
02:01:42,264 --> 02:01:44,334
Look at you, Gencebey.

894
02:01:44,577 --> 02:01:49,027
You went to your homelands.
You caught up with your parents.

895
02:01:49,333 --> 02:01:53,383
You rode your horse from Karabağ
to here to fight in battle.

896
02:01:54,599 --> 02:01:56,999
Don't you ever get tired?

897
02:01:57,485 --> 02:02:01,255
Thank you, Cerkutay. Thank you.
Now I'm catching up with my brothers.

898
02:02:02,656 --> 02:02:05,456
I missed fighting alongside my bey.

899
02:02:06,778 --> 02:02:11,297
Until our horses die and our blood
gets dry, we are behind Osman Bey.

900
02:02:11,297 --> 02:02:12,507
Thank you.

901
02:02:16,578 --> 02:02:19,018
Harmankaya Castle

902
02:02:20,261 --> 02:02:22,031
Osman.

903
02:02:25,234 --> 02:02:27,514
I said this is it.

904
02:02:29,498 --> 02:02:32,008
I said this is it.
This is it.

905
02:02:33,044 --> 02:02:38,814
Then again, again, again he ran
away from me. Again!

906
02:02:40,503 --> 02:02:42,493
How could he?

907
02:02:42,898 --> 02:02:44,618
Tell me, Nikola!

908
02:02:45,163 --> 02:02:49,893
From that ambush, among all those
soldiers, how did he get out alive?

909
02:02:50,147 --> 02:02:52,827
I wounded him deeply, Kosses!

910
02:02:53,336 --> 02:02:56,636
I said I won't return before seeing
him dead!

911
02:02:56,828 --> 02:02:59,008
And I didn't!

912
02:02:59,008 --> 02:03:01,718
I followed him for a day!

913
02:03:02,405 --> 02:03:06,405
Then, then he faced me...

914
02:03:08,102 --> 02:03:09,962
and fought.

915
02:03:15,033 --> 02:03:17,133
This man isn't dying.

916
02:03:18,788 --> 02:03:21,698
He isn't dying.
He isn't.

917
02:03:22,059 --> 02:03:24,296
He isn't dying, Kosses.
He isn't.

918
02:03:24,296 --> 02:03:27,106
Nikola, we thought of this
possibility.

919
02:03:27,767 --> 02:03:33,407
When he returns, the funerals of
his loved ones will be waiting.

920
02:03:36,293 --> 02:03:41,113
I swore an oath. He will feel
that pain before dying.

921
02:03:41,265 --> 02:03:43,415
He won't!

922
02:03:46,924 --> 02:03:48,964
He won't die.

923
02:03:52,386 --> 02:03:56,336
Of course, I also thought that Osman
could run away.

924
02:03:58,029 --> 02:04:00,799
I have a spy in İznik.

925
02:04:03,225 --> 02:04:06,225
The woman is working in the governor's
kitchen.

926
02:04:09,975 --> 02:04:12,975
And she knows that Osman is coming.

927
02:04:15,995 --> 02:04:19,495
She is very talented with poisons.

928
02:04:23,026 --> 02:04:27,806
I gave her a lot of gold for her to
prepare a good ending for Osman.

929
02:04:47,624 --> 02:04:50,084
Possibilities, Rogatus.

930
02:04:52,063 --> 02:04:54,573
Possibilities, Kosses.

931
02:04:58,558 --> 02:05:01,468
You never give up, Nikola.

932
02:05:02,290 --> 02:05:06,290
This makes you a scary enemy...

933
02:05:07,388 --> 02:05:11,858
and a good ally.

934
02:05:12,570 --> 02:05:15,500
We tried it many times with
swords.

935
02:05:16,255 --> 02:05:19,065
I couldn't let him live anymore.

936
02:05:19,397 --> 02:05:23,257
Tell us, Nikola.
What poison is this?

937
02:05:23,651 --> 02:05:28,671
It's a poison strong enough to kill a
horse in a very short time.

938
02:05:29,465 --> 02:05:32,525
Even a horse!

939
02:05:41,241 --> 02:05:44,261
İznik Castle

940
02:05:54,141 --> 02:05:56,669
Now we passed the merchants and
the lords, my bey.

941
02:05:56,669 --> 02:05:59,289
We used to give the governor
a carpet before.

942
02:05:59,577 --> 02:06:02,417
Now, we are providing all
his needs.

943
02:06:02,612 --> 02:06:07,772
When he sends his caravans safely,
it'll be heard from everywhere.

944
02:06:08,250 --> 02:06:13,160
They'll hear that our lands are safe.

945
02:06:13,899 --> 02:06:15,749
We have prosperity.

946
02:06:17,875 --> 02:06:20,055
We are growing day by day, Osman Bey.

947
02:06:21,998 --> 02:06:25,948
May Allah destine you and your
lineage even better days.

948
02:06:27,028 --> 02:06:29,658
Amin, Malhun. Amin.

949
02:06:44,960 --> 02:06:48,220
I wouldn't let you go like this,
Osman Bey.

950
02:06:48,284 --> 02:06:51,504
And also, we need to celebrate
our agreement.

951
02:07:10,812 --> 02:07:12,452
Go on.

952
02:07:30,722 --> 02:07:32,282
Go on.

953
02:08:15,642 --> 02:08:17,732
Sadaqallahulazim.

954
02:09:03,154 --> 02:09:05,384
Soon, my Orhan.

955
02:09:05,598 --> 02:09:08,748
Soon you will reunite with your
mother and father.

956
02:11:34,754 --> 02:11:37,269
-Salam Alaikum.
-Alaikum Salam.

957
02:11:37,269 --> 02:11:41,079
It's not the time for a change of guards.
What is this, brothers?

958
02:11:42,551 --> 02:11:44,361
Who are you?

959
02:13:30,840 --> 02:13:32,680
Didn't you like it?

960
02:13:43,929 --> 02:13:46,299
Sherbets are here.

961
02:14:03,604 --> 02:14:06,084
Now, we are friends, Osman Bey.

962
02:14:07,783 --> 02:14:11,763
Everything on the table is made
according to your religion's rules.

963
02:14:15,686 --> 02:14:19,896
All the meat is bought from
Muslim butchers.

964
02:14:25,723 --> 02:14:27,283
Please.

965
02:14:27,616 --> 02:14:29,106
Go on.

966
02:14:33,805 --> 02:14:36,365
If you say that it's halal.

967
02:14:40,159 --> 02:14:42,039
Then...

968
02:14:47,569 --> 02:14:49,479
Let us enjoy it.

969
02:14:54,298 --> 02:14:56,268
With the name of Allah.

970
02:14:57,159 --> 02:14:59,149
Thank you, my bey.

971
02:14:59,400 --> 02:15:00,810
Thank you, my bey.

972
02:15:04,521 --> 02:15:06,561
I also want Sherbet.

973
02:15:12,334 --> 02:15:13,874
Come on.
With the name of Allah.

974
02:16:34,442 --> 02:16:36,323
Where is this?

975
02:17:11,835 --> 02:17:14,096
So, you were protecting it.

976
02:19:28,156 --> 02:19:30,755
I will kill you all!

977
02:21:04,170 --> 02:21:15,250
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com